  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently we can scan avatars and for the most part see what makes them up. However as an avatar world creator I can see the scanner used for worlds is more advanced and sees everything in an avatar. My suggestion would be use the world scanner on every avatar that's uploaded and have it also run on every avatar that is uploaded from here on out. That data could then be collected into a massive database where the game cross references it instead of live scanning every avatar. This would save network congestion and help bring the new IK back which was removed due to Network lag. Also when the scan is done it could even see and detect crash avatars and delete them or flag them for deletion/inspection perhaps which would help people getting crashed by cancerous avatars. Perhaps have it so that if an avatar has over 50k Particles or detects meshes over 500k total.",
